 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "West Wind, bring to us a delicate wind\nFrom the boundless deeps of the ages gone,\nAnd with it let our hearts be confident\nOf what shall come and when; promise\nThe present night that is forever.\nAnd tell us, as thy warm wings breathe above\nOur shuddering souls again\nLit by heaven's first brightness\nUnheeded in their wake then left behind,\nWhere once for ever was not buried.\nMarching on those winds of glory,\nLet there be no east weather",
